import{_ as t,o,c as n,ag as r}from"./chunks/framework.cyF4XceO.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Private intent snapshots in a Runner","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"docs/provider-private-snapshot-backend.md","filePath":"docs/provider-private-snapshot-backend.md"}'),i={name:"docs/provider-private-snapshot-backend.md"};function a(s,e,d,c,l,u){return o(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="private-intent-snapshots-in-a-runner" tabindex="-1">Private intent snapshots in a Runner <a class="header-anchor" href="#private-intent-snapshots-in-a-runner" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Private intent snapshots in a Runner&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The v2 Host Provider has two explicit, mutually exclusive intent-store modes:</p><ul><li><code>store_path</code> opens an already initialized private filesystem store. Its <code>Initialize</code>/<code>InitializeBound</code> and <code>Open</code> behavior is unchanged; Configure never creates or adopts a missing local path.</li><li><code>intent_store_slot</code> selects an opaque private file supplied by the Runner. The Provider also requires <code>store_id</code> and <code>host_api_root</code>. The slot is not a Host resource or a storage-provider selection. It is never inferred from the Host endpoint, Workspace, Run ID or product name.</li></ul><p>For remote mode, the Runner supplies exactly one private descriptor source. <code>TAKOSUMI_PRIVATE_RUN_FILES_FILE</code> names an absolute file in a private, Runner-owned directory. Its complete JSON envelope has this shape: <code>{&quot;version&quot;:1,&quot;sequence&quot;:0,&quot;files&quot;:[{&quot;slot&quot;:&quot;...&quot;,&quot;endpoint&quot;:&quot;...&quot;,&quot;grant&quot;:&quot;...&quot;}]}</code>. The Provider validates version 1 and a sequence no greater than 2048, then atomically pins the first observed sequence, bytes, and slot/endpoint set. It reopens and validates the file before every read, commit, and receipt resolve; it accepts an exact same-sequence replay, rejects rollback or changed bytes at the same sequence, and permits an increased sequence only with the same slot/endpoint set. The Runner should atomically replace its 0600 regular file with an increasing sequence when it renews grants. No grant is cached from this file. The envelope is limited to 4 MiB and 256 slots.</p><p>The original <code>TAKOSUMI_PRIVATE_RUN_FILES</code> JSON array of <code>{ &quot;slot&quot;: &quot;...&quot;, &quot;endpoint&quot;: &quot;...&quot;, &quot;grant&quot;: &quot;...&quot; }</code> remains an explicit, nonrenewed process input. It cannot be combined with the file input; an invalid file never falls back to the static array. In either mode, the selected endpoint is the exact internal base <code>/internal/private-run-files/v1</code>; the Provider sends <code>POST</code> requests to its <code>/read</code>, <code>/commit</code> and <code>/resolve</code> children with the opaque grant as a Bearer header. HTTPS is required except for an explicitly loopback HTTP endpoint for local/self-hosted integration. Redirects are never followed. The environment value, file path and grant are process inputs only: none is included in an intent snapshot, Terraform state, a Host request, or a diagnostic.</p><p><code>read</code> returns an absent marker or <code>{kind:&quot;present&quot;,version,digest,bytesBase64}</code>. The Provider verifies the SHA-256 digest and runs the existing strict snapshot/store-ID/Host-binding validation before it interprets any intent. For an absent slot only, Configure conditionally writes an empty snapshot at expected version zero. A concurrent initializer may win; the loser accepts only a subsequently read, valid snapshot with the same store ID and exact Host binding. Foreign or malformed custody is never reset or overwritten.</p><p>Every subsequent mutation reads the current version, applies the same <code>intentv2.Store</code> business rules as local mode, and commits the new snapshot with that expected version and a fresh commit ID. The Provider returns an intent, including its original Host idempotency key, only after an exact commit receipt is acknowledged. If a commit response is lost or unknown, it issues one <code>/resolve</code> for that exact commit ID, expected version and digest. In file mode, this resolve reopens the current descriptor and may use a newer grant; it never retries the original commit. Only an exact committed receipt qualifies. Conflict or unresolved outcomes return a value-free error and do not authorize a Host send or a blind mutation retry. A competing writer can therefore produce one winner, not two Host claims. The snapshot limit is 16 MiB decoded.</p><p>The Core, not this Provider, enforces grant scope, current Run lease and execution-authority epoch in its atomic private-file commit. This backend is an internal Runner custody integration; it does not change a published Host API, Form, or Provider resource state schema. It does not by itself prove Runner dispatch, Cloud D1/R2 durability, or production readiness.</p>',8)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",a]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
